  "result": "Perfect! All 170 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement functionality:\n\n\u2705 **Created src/statements.js** with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function:\n\nReturns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` where:\n- **customerId**: normalized customer ID\n- **invoices**: filtered and formatted list of customer invoices with:\n  - `number`: invoice number (or 'DRAFT' if missing)\n  - `issueDate`: invoice issue date\n  - `dueDate`: payment due date (or 'N/A' if missing)\n  - `total`: invoice total (subtotal - discount + VAT - voucher)\n  - `due`: amount still owed (from balanceDue)\n- **totalDue**: sum of all due amounts\n\n**Filtering criteria:**\n- Only invoices for the specified customer\n- Status must be 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n- issueDate must be on or before asOf\n- Sorted by issueDate (ascending)\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND for unknown customers\n- Normalizes customer IDs (trim, uppercase)\n\n\u2705 **12 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Empty statements for customers with no issued invoices\n- Filtering by customer, status, and date\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Invoice detail inclusion (number, dates, totals)\n- Due amount calculation with partial payments\n- Total due summation\n- Customer ID normalization\n- Edge cases (missing number shows DRAFT, missing dueDate shows N/A)\n\nCustomer statements are now fully implemented with proper filtering, sorting, and total calculations.",
